The easiest way to remember
VERTEX AI = WHERE you build/run AI

PIPELINE = HOW a predefined workflow runs

AI AGENT = WHO/WHAT intelligently works toward a goal
Your Business Consultant AI example

Your project can be understood as:

👤 User
   ↓
💬 Business Consultant AI Chat Interface
   ↓
🧠 AI Agent
   ↓
☁️ Vertex AI / Agent Engine
   ↓
🤖 Gemini Model
   ↓
💡 Business Advice

If you later add business data analysis and a repeatable model-training workflow, you could also use a Vertex AI Pipeline:

Business Data
   ↓
🔄 Vertex AI Pipeline
   ↓
Prepare Data → Train → Evaluate
   ↓
🧠 Trained Model
   ↓
Deploy / Use in AI Application

So, they can work together: Vertex AI is the platform, a Pipeline handles structured workflows, and an AI Agent handles intelligent goal-based tasks.

